### A8 — FIX LOSS AGGREGATION FOR WEIGHTED CROSS-ENTROPY (ALL 6 NOTEBOOKS)

Replace per-step loss accumulation in the training loop with correct averaging:

```python
# CORRECT pattern:
train_loss_sum = 0.0
train_correct = 0
train_total = 0

for batch_idx, (inputs, targets) in enumerate(train_loader):
    if SMOKE_TEST and batch_idx >= SMOKE_BATCHES:
        break
    inputs, targets = inputs.to(DEVICE), targets.to(DEVICE)
    optimizer.zero_grad()
    with torch.cuda.amp.autocast():
        outputs = model(inputs)
        loss = criterion(outputs, targets)
    scaler.scale(loss).backward()
    scaler.unscale_(optimizer)
    torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), GRAD_CLIP)
    scaler.step(optimizer)
    scaler.update()
    
    # Accumulate as float (detached), not calling .item() every step
    train_loss_sum += loss.detach().float() * inputs.size(0)
    preds = outputs.detach().argmax(1)
    train_correct += (preds == targets).sum()
    train_total += inputs.size(0)

# After loop — single .item() call per epoch:
train_loss = (train_loss_sum / train_total).item()
train_acc  = (train_correct / train_total).item()
```

